      "status": "fail",
      "evidence": "judge: 0/3 blind judges pass. Phase 4 commit 72f79d7 (Tasks: T7, T8) mixes unrelated concerns. It adds tests/test_acceptance.py (417 lines). It also changes server.py (request_queue_size=128), store.py (moves PRAGMA user_version after the schema statements) and __main__.py (docstring and unconditional client import), plus a conftest Proc stderr-to-file change. Phase 3 commit 37931be (T5, T6) bundles the serve command (__main__.py, test_serve.py) with a separate client CLI (client.py, test_client.py), and its subject says 'serve ... and client CLI'. Phase 2 commit f13204f (T3+T4) is defensible, since server.py holds both and the message says so, and the tracking files in the chore and notes commits are fine under the Q5/D97 precedent. 72f79d7 and 37931be still fall short of the protocol's 'split into multiple small logically-grouped commits, one concern per commit' (execution-protocol.md:44, step 16). Phases 2-4 each got a single functional commit, so about 2 of the 5 functional commits are multi-concern. Commits 8f57795, 4f48861, ff20572, 19fa925, bf81a08, the chore(phase-N) commits and 5ee75ce are each one concern."
    },
